The U.K.'s position as one of the world's biggest entertainment hubs is being given a boost by UTA , which is relocating its London headquarters to a new purpose-built space and bring with it all its local businesses.

According to the agency, the move &#x2014;&#xA0;set to take place in early 2027 &#x2014;&#xA0;shows its "unwavering commitment to the U.K. market as a cornerstone of its global growth strategy, further reinforcing its long-term international ambitions and expanding footprint across EMEA." It added that, by bringing it staff across London together it hopes "create new opportunities for clients, further connect talent and IP across disciplines, and deliver a more joined-up approach to representation." blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

The Frank Gehry-designed central London location at One Rathbone Square,&#xA0;a 70,000 square feet across two floors space, will house UTA alongside talent agency Curtis Brown, which it acquired in 2022, and global soccer agency ROOF, which it bought in 2024. The offices were formerly occupied by Meta until it scaled-backed the number of its London bases in recent years.

&#x201C;This move represents our commitment to our UK presence and the role it will play in UTA&#x2019;s future globally," said UTA's Darnell Strom, who moved over from the U.S. last year to head up U.K. operations. "Bringing UTA, Curtis Brown and ROOF together in one place will allow our teams to collaborate in new ways and deliver even more opportunities for our clients, as we connect that talent with the full reach of UTA&#x2019;s global network.&#x201D;

UTA's U.K. client list includes the likes of Michaela Coel, Paapa Essiedu, Lily James, Richard Gadd, Ncuti Gatwa and "Industry" creators Mickey Down and Konrad Kay.

EXCLUSIVE: Artist and filmmaker Allison Janae Hamilton has set her next project, a narrative short titled Holler, starring musician Valerie June. The film will be produced under Hamilton&#x2019;s newly minted production company, Swampwife Pictures .

Set against the rural landscape of West Tennessee, the film follows a hard-living Memphis nightclub owner who returns to her family&#x2019;s land when signs of a once-in-a-generation ecological event begin to emerge. Called home to perform a ritual demanded by her lineage, she must confront both the ancestral responsibilities she has inherited and the person she left behind without saying goodbye. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories News Allison Janae Hamilton Discusses Her Latest Film Project 'Venus Of Ossabaw' & How She Plans To Reach Audiences In The "Popular Arena" With Her Debut Feature 'Floridaland' News Rotterdam Hires Pepijn Kuyper As Managing Director

