Hamilton is a 2026 Guggenheim Fellow. Her previous short film, Venus of Ossabaw , debuted in March 2026 at Telfair Museums in Savannah, Georgia. She is currently adapting the short into a feature. Hamilton is also in development on Floridaland , another feature script she has penned. The project was selected as part of the Sundance Institute&#x2019;s 2026 Screenwriters Intensive.

&#x201C;The elements that these films have in common form the cornerstone of what I want to do with Swampwife, which is to tell stories rooted in the land, driven by character, and that expand our ideas of genre,&#x201D; Hamilton told Deadline .

&#x201C;I want Swampwife to be known for stories that feel like stepping into another world, one of richly layered visuals and emotionally resonant characters. Swampwife gives all my storytelling interests a single home.&#x201D;

