Netflix &#x2019;s feature-length documentary &#x201C; Tyson Fury ,&#x201D; which follows the two-time heavyweight champion of the world&#x2019;s journey from childhood to the pinnacle of his sport, reveals that the boxer has been diagnosed with schizophrenia.

The film, which is directed by Lucy Wilcox, will debut on Nov. 27, just two weeks before Fury&#x2019;s live Netflix bout against Anthony Joshua.

The film charts the triumphs and setbacks of his career, his struggles with mental health and addiction, the loss of a child, complex family relationships and the question of what it means to be a man. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

It includes conversations with Fury, his wife Paris and his father John - compiled over six months and 27 hours - alongside never-before-seen archive footage.

The film shows Fury discovering and meeting his half-brothers Tommy and Roman, the turning point in 2017, and the impact of his father&#x2019;s imprisonment.

Discussing his schizophrenia diagnosis, Fury says: &#x201C;Words can&#x2019;t explain the darkness I was in. I came from the living version of the pits of hellfire. And I 100% thought at times I'd end up in a padded room with the door locked, and that scared me so much.

&#x201C;I was waking up in the night like this, the anxiety was crippling me. I just could not overcome it. Completely gone, and that&#x2019;s when I went and saw the psychiatrist down in London. She asked me like a gazillion questions and stuff, and I ticked all the boxes, whatever was going on. Depression, anxiety, bipolar disorder&#x2026;&#x201D;

Paris Fury adds: &#x201C;He's a mild schizophrenic and even then the penny didn't drop. It was like, don't be silly. What's she on about? Schizophrenic, maniacs are schizophrenic. You're not schizophrenic, you know?&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

